Expanded story:
Amy stirred eggs on a sunny kitchen counter while Will and Amber giggled over pancakes, the scent of butter filling the small home. The front door slammed open; a zombie lunged in, its rotting fingers reaching for her. She grabbed Will’s hand, pulled him toward the back stairwell, then scooped up Amber into her arms as they ran to the basement safe room. Amy sprinted back through the hallway, heart pounding, and slotted the kitchen counter down for cover. In the pantry she found a hidden pocket: a pistol gleamed beside a katana blade; she drew them with shaking fingers. One by one zombies crashed at the door—she fired the pistol, then sliced with the katana, each strike sending bodies to the floor. New undead surged from every crack in the walls. The last zombie staggered and fell as Amy’s final shot rang out. Breathing hard, she pushed open the basement hatch and carried Will and Amber back into her kitchen.
